WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:02.169
The Woman in the House
Across the Street

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:03.587
from the Girl in the Window

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.713
features a lot of wine,

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:06.632
a lot of broken
casserole dishes,

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:08.634
and a lot of
shocking revelations.

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:10.260
This video
is here to explain

00:00:10.344 --> 00:00:12.471
all those twists and turns,

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:14.640
so make sure you've
watched the series first.

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:15.933
There are lots
of spoilers to come.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.267
No!

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:18.310
With that in mind,

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:21.104
time to pour
two massive glasses of red

00:00:21.188 --> 00:00:22.731
and get down to business.

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:28.654
Anna sees
a woman being murdered

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.697
in the window in the house
across the street -

00:00:30.781 --> 00:00:32.741
don't worry,
I won't keep saying that.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:34.535
The woman is Lisa Maines,

00:00:34.618 --> 00:00:36.495
the air hostess girlfriend
of Neil,

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:38.580
who is the handsome dad
who has just moved in

00:00:38.664 --> 00:00:39.998
to the house across...

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:42.376
No. The property
opposite Anna's.

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:45.337
Anna is settling in for
her nightly pint of wine,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.714
when she sees
Lisa with her throat cut.

00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:50.259
Problem is,
when the police turn up,

00:00:50.342 --> 00:00:51.635
there's no blood or body,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.971
and Neil says
Lisa is out of town

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.764
in her job
as an air hostess.

00:00:56.473 --> 00:00:58.684
What follows is six episodes
of red herrings,

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.103
to go with
all that red wine.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.565
Neil's past is littered
with dead women,

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:06.483
which we'll explain
in a second,

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.152
but he's also seen
carrying a body in a sack.

00:01:09.653 --> 00:01:10.571
Oh my God.

00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:13.240
Which turns out to be
a ventriloquist's dummy.

00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:15.492
Might actually be
more creepy than a body.

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:16.743
It's my
ventriloquist's dummy.

00:01:16.827 --> 00:01:17.953
What?

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:20.831
Then there's Rex,
arrested in episode six,

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.916
once the police
find Lisa's body.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.334
Turns out
he was under surveillance

00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:25.544
for a different crime

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:27.713
and was recorded
threatening to kill Lisa.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.674
I swear to God, Chastity,
I'm gonna fucking kill you.

00:01:31.258 --> 00:01:32.968
I'm gonna cut you
into little pieces

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:34.303
so they can't find--

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:37.222
Again, we can explain
that one in a minute.

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:40.267
The biggest red herring
of them all is Anna herself.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.435
Lisa's body was found

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:43.061
near one of the painter's
palette knives.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.230
And to make matters worse,

00:01:45.314 --> 00:01:47.274
she had accidentally
brandished the knife

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:49.735
at Carol
in an earlier episode.

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:50.944
You stop telling people that

00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:52.654
-I have a drinking problem.
-Anna!

00:01:52.738 --> 00:01:54.448
And was seen having
an argument with Lisa.

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:56.950
You know what?
Let me call you back.

00:01:57.451 --> 00:01:59.328
We know it was
about her throwing away

00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:00.537
smelly colouring pens,

00:02:00.621 --> 00:02:03.457
but to the outside world,
it looked like a threat.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.212
This in turn
unlocks a memory in Anna

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:10.380
of stabbing Lisa
with the palette knife.

00:02:11.632 --> 00:02:14.384
And there's blood dripping
down from the attic.

00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:16.887
The solution
is a bit more innocent.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:17.763
Oh my God.

00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:19.389
The blood is red paint,

00:02:20.432 --> 00:02:21.725
and her memory
comes from slashing

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.851
at a painting of Lisa.

00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:27.064
As we see early on,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.025
Anna's trauma prevents her
from finishing any painting,

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:32.486
and makes her destroy
her half-finished attempts.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.321
She no more murdered Lisa

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:36.740
than she murdered
these flowers.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.452
I didn't stab her.

00:02:40.536 --> 00:02:41.912
I didn't kill anybody.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.789
Okay, maybe
it's a bit sinister

00:02:43.872 --> 00:02:45.499
that she was painting
pictures of Lisa

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:46.583
in the first place,

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:49.294
but it's better than
being an actual murderer.

00:02:49.378 --> 00:02:51.088
No, the shocking reveal

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.090
is that it was
Neil's daughter Emma

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.967
who was responsible
all along,

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.927
driven to a murderous rage

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.555
by Lisa's refusal
to buy her chocolate bars.

00:02:59.638 --> 00:03:00.514
Emma?

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.350
People always
underestimate children.

00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:05.519
Underestimate
what they're capable of.

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:07.604
We can't be
the only ones who got chills

00:03:07.688 --> 00:03:08.814
from her transformation,

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:11.942
from young entrepreneur
to violent maniac.

00:03:15.362 --> 00:03:17.281
Emma then stole
Anna's palette knife

00:03:17.364 --> 00:03:19.533
when she was distracted
getting her chequebook,

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:20.993
and used that to frame her.

00:03:21.076 --> 00:03:22.035
And if you're wondering

00:03:22.119 --> 00:03:23.495
why Neil
didn't suspect anything?

00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:26.123
Well, he missed
the murder itself

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.000
because he was
practising ventriloquism

00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:29.126
in the bathroom.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.795
But what about
her absence after that?

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:33.881
As Detective Lane
explained earlier,

00:03:33.964 --> 00:03:36.341
it would be easy for someone
to take Lisa's phone

00:03:36.425 --> 00:03:38.385
and text
fake messages to Neil.

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:39.970
I'm sure
he has a phone somewhere.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.597
Texted himself an alibi,

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.098
sent all those texts
to Neil.

00:03:43.182 --> 00:03:45.684
Neil also thought
Lisa was flying to Seattle

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:46.852
as an air hostess.

00:03:46.935 --> 00:03:49.813
But, as we discover,
she wasn't an air hostess.

00:03:49.897 --> 00:03:51.773
The airline in question,
Olympia,

00:03:51.857 --> 00:03:54.234
doesn't even fly
to the West Coast.

00:03:54.318 --> 00:03:56.361
And because Lisa
was lying about her job,

00:03:56.445 --> 00:04:00.324
it made it all the more easy
for Emma to hide her murder.

00:04:03.827 --> 00:04:05.495
Of course,
that first question

00:04:05.579 --> 00:04:07.956
should maybe be,
"Who killed Chastity?"

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.834
Yes, it turns out Lisa
was living a double life,

00:04:10.918 --> 00:04:13.378
working with
her partner in crime, Rex,

00:04:13.462 --> 00:04:14.963
to scam rich men.

00:04:15.047 --> 00:04:17.466
And Neil was
just their next target.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.261
Anna had her suspicions
way back in episode two,

00:04:21.345 --> 00:04:23.347
where she discovered
that Lisa was being followed

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.724
by a mysterious account
on Instagram

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:27.601
called Sexy Rexy.

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:30.854
Look at this.
Fire emoji, fire emoji.

00:04:30.938 --> 00:04:33.857
Eggplant emo--
Eggplant emoji?

00:04:33.941 --> 00:04:35.984
Do you know what
an eggplant emoji means?

00:04:36.068 --> 00:04:37.152
-Yes.
-It means a dick.

00:04:37.236 --> 00:04:40.072
At the time, Anna thought
Lisa was having an affair,

00:04:40.155 --> 00:04:41.990
but it's
more complicated than that.

00:04:42.491 --> 00:04:44.201
Lisa is actually Chastity,

00:04:44.785 --> 00:04:46.245
a bartender
at the strip club

00:04:46.328 --> 00:04:48.163
where Rex works as a dancer.

00:04:48.664 --> 00:04:51.041
When the two meet,
she draws him into a scheme.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:53.252
She targets
recently widowed men,

00:04:53.335 --> 00:04:55.504
and tricks them into
starting a relationship,

00:04:55.587 --> 00:04:57.840
before introducing Rex
as her sick brother

00:04:57.923 --> 00:04:59.716
in order to scam
money out of them

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.218
for a fake operation.

00:05:01.802 --> 00:05:03.595
They're pulling off
the scam with Neil

00:05:03.679 --> 00:05:05.889
when Lisa/Chastity
is murdered,

00:05:05.973 --> 00:05:08.559
which is why Rex turns up
on Anna's doorstep,

00:05:08.642 --> 00:05:10.561
before moving
to Anna's stairs,

00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:13.063
shower and kitchen worktop.

00:05:17.025 --> 00:05:18.902
One reason
Anna is suspicious of Neil

00:05:18.986 --> 00:05:20.737
is because when
she looks into his past,

00:05:20.821 --> 00:05:22.155
she finds a trail of bodies.

00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:24.867
-Oh my God.
-Well, two bodies.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.451
I think
that counts as a trail.

00:05:26.952 --> 00:05:28.453
There's Neil's wife,
Meredith,

00:05:28.537 --> 00:05:29.913
allegedly
drowned in the lake,

00:05:29.997 --> 00:05:32.916
and Maxine, Emma's teacher,
who fell off a cliff

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.335
during a school trip
chaperoned by Neil.

00:05:36.295 --> 00:05:37.754
Neil was
the only adult present

00:05:37.838 --> 00:05:39.006
at both crime scenes,

00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:41.466
which leads to Anna
picturing him as the killer.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.468
Of course, the only
other person at both scenes

00:05:43.552 --> 00:05:45.971
was Emma herself,
and as we now know,

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:49.266
this kid is not as sweet as
the chocolate she's selling.

00:05:50.726 --> 00:05:52.436
Jealous of
the second child on the way,

00:05:52.519 --> 00:05:56.440
she killed her pregnant mum
by sabotaging the lake pier.

00:05:57.107 --> 00:05:59.318
She also pushed her teacher
from the lighthouse

00:05:59.401 --> 00:06:00.861
for reasons unknown.

00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:03.197
There's a surprising amount
of upper body strength

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.323
in that tiny kid.

00:06:08.994 --> 00:06:10.579
Throughout
The Woman in the House,

00:06:10.662 --> 00:06:11.496
Anna is convinced

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.832
there's something bad
happening in the attic.

00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:15.209
Hello?

00:06:15.292 --> 00:06:16.210
She hears creaks,

00:06:16.293 --> 00:06:17.753
and we see a shadowy figure

00:06:17.836 --> 00:06:19.296
at the end
of the first episode.

00:06:20.214 --> 00:06:23.091
Again, it's all
a harmless misunderstanding.

00:06:23.175 --> 00:06:24.968
Well, as harmless
as having a handyman

00:06:25.052 --> 00:06:27.262
secretly living
in your loft can be.

00:06:27.346 --> 00:06:29.431
Buell has been
living up here.

00:06:29.515 --> 00:06:30.641
Yes, turns out that

00:06:30.724 --> 00:06:33.435
friendly Buell has been
sleeping in the rafters.

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:35.521
It's easy to suspect
the DIY expert

00:06:35.604 --> 00:06:37.105
of being up to no good.

00:06:37.189 --> 00:06:39.024
Not only has he spent
several years

00:06:39.107 --> 00:06:40.150
fixing that mailbox,

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:42.402
but he's played
by Cameron Britton,

00:06:42.486 --> 00:06:43.737
forever associated
in our heads

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.906
as the terrifying Ed Kemper

00:06:45.989 --> 00:06:48.325
in Netflix serial-killer
drama Mindhunter.

00:06:48.951 --> 00:06:49.785
Thankfully,

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:52.663
his only crime here
is being a very slow worker,

00:06:53.163 --> 00:06:55.374
and maybe some
inappropriate taxidermy.

00:07:01.171 --> 00:07:03.006
The show ends
with a final twist

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.801
as Anna flies out
to New York one year later.

00:07:05.884 --> 00:07:07.219
-Red or white?
-Oh.

00:07:07.302 --> 00:07:09.847
No, thank you.
I don't drink wine anymore.

00:07:10.347 --> 00:07:11.181
I'll have a vodka.

00:07:13.475 --> 00:07:15.686
She sits next to
a mysterious businesswoman,

00:07:15.769 --> 00:07:17.479
played by
film legend Glenn Close,

00:07:17.563 --> 00:07:20.065
and accidentally
drinks herself into a stupor

00:07:20.148 --> 00:07:22.734
by mixing vodka
with a Xanax prescription.

00:07:23.235 --> 00:07:24.486
She wakes up,

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.405
finds Glenn Close's body
in the toilets,

00:07:26.989 --> 00:07:30.117
only for the body to vanish
when she alerts the crew.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.494
Yes, it's almost
the same setup as the murder

00:07:32.578 --> 00:07:33.912
that kicked the show off.

00:07:33.996 --> 00:07:35.789
Let's get you
back to your seat.

00:07:35.873 --> 00:07:38.417
Though this time, not only
has the body gone missing,

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.334
but the crew claim

00:07:39.418 --> 00:07:40.919
there wasn't
a passenger in the seat

00:07:41.003 --> 00:07:41.879
to begin with.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.840
There was no one in seat 2A.

00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:46.884
Just as the police thought

00:07:46.967 --> 00:07:48.427
Anna was imagining
Lisa's murder,

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.762
based on the book
she was reading at the time,

00:07:50.846 --> 00:07:52.306
The Woman Across the Lake,

00:07:52.389 --> 00:07:54.224
Anna is now reading
the sequel,

00:07:54.308 --> 00:07:55.726
The Girl on the Cruise.

00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:57.978
If you look carefully
at the blurb on the back,

00:07:58.061 --> 00:07:59.438
it's the same story as hers.

00:08:00.022 --> 00:08:01.523
Having survived one mystery,

00:08:01.607 --> 00:08:02.816
the heroine takes a trip,

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:05.444
only for a lady to vanish
from the boat she's on.

00:08:05.527 --> 00:08:07.446
Is this
Anna's mind playing tricks,

00:08:07.529 --> 00:08:09.531
or a setup for a sequel?

00:08:09.615 --> 00:08:10.908
One thing is for sure:

00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:13.619
after eight episodes
of pitch-perfect parody,

00:08:13.702 --> 00:08:15.162
we'd devour some more.

00:08:15.245 --> 00:08:16.371
Bingo.

00:08:17.247 --> 00:08:20.083
And so we reach the end of -
deep breath -

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:21.919
The Woman in the House
Across the Street

00:08:22.002 --> 00:08:23.128
from the Girl in the Window.

00:08:23.795 --> 00:08:25.881
Who knew a comedy
could keep us this gripped?

00:08:25.964 --> 00:08:28.300
If you're looking to see
how accurate the parody is,

00:08:28.383 --> 00:08:29.593
you could check out

00:08:29.676 --> 00:08:31.261
The Woman in the Window
on Netflix.

00:08:31.345 --> 00:08:33.180
And if you enjoyed
this breakdown,

00:08:33.263 --> 00:08:35.015
subscribe
to Still Watching Netflix

00:08:35.098 --> 00:08:36.683
for more videos like it.

